# {{.Name}}

This project uses Modary's Governed Profile for high-impact operations that
need authorization, Preview, idempotency, audit, and transactionally enqueued
background work. The complete selection is visible in
`internal/project/project.go`:

- governed PostgreSQL plus River;
- local development Identity and bearer authentication;
- RBAC and SQL Audit;
- the consumer-owned `limits.set` Action and `limits.changed` task;
- CLI, HTTP Action API, and MCP transports.

The generated project has no Admin UI. Local Identity is a development adapter;
replace it at the composition root before production deployment.

## Configure

Use one PostgreSQL database and two schemas. River uses the queue schema; a
separate database is not required. Use lowercase ASCII identifiers; the
application schema is at most 63 bytes and the queue schema is at most 46 bytes.
Generated defaults use project-derived role prefixes, keeping application,
queue, and test namespaces distinct and outside PostgreSQL's reserved schemas.
Overlong names retain a readable prefix and add a deterministic hash fragment
within those limits.

```sh
export DATABASE_URL='postgres://user:password@127.0.0.1:5432/app?sslmode=disable'
export MODARY_APPLICATION_SCHEMA={{.SchemaID}}
export MODARY_QUEUE_SCHEMA={{.QueueSchemaID}}
export MODARY_OPERATOR_USERNAME=operator
export MODARY_OPERATOR_PASSWORD='replace-with-at-least-12-characters'
export MODARY_OPERATOR_TOKEN='replace-with-at-least-32-random-characters'
export MODARY_ALLOW_INSECURE_COOKIE=true # local HTTP only
```

Apply the selected forward migrations once before Preview, Execute, serving,
or worker startup:

```sh
go run ./cmd/{{.ID}} migrate
```

Serving and commands do not apply migrations unless
`MODARY_MIGRATE_ON_START=true` is selected explicitly for a controlled local
workflow.

## Preview And Execute

Create `input.json` and a mode-0600 token file:

```json
{"value": 25, "expected_version": 0}
```

```sh
printf '%s' "$MODARY_OPERATOR_TOKEN" > token
chmod 600 token
go run ./cmd/{{.ID}} action run limits.set \
  --token-file token --input input.json --scope-kind workspace --scope-id default \
  --preview --request-id preview-1
```

The Preview response contains `plan_hash`. Execute the exact input with that
hash and a stable idempotency key:

```sh
go run ./cmd/{{.ID}} action run limits.set \
  --token-file token --input input.json --scope-kind workspace --scope-id default \
  --plan 'sha256:...' \
  --idempotency-key limit-default-v1 --request-id execute-1
```

## Serve And Work

Run the session-authenticated Action API, health endpoint, and MCP endpoint:

```sh
go run ./cmd/{{.ID}} serve --listen 127.0.0.1:8080
```

Run durable work in a separate process:

```sh
go run ./cmd/{{.ID}}-worker
```

`internal/limits/worker.go` validates the durable event. Replace the generated
callback in the worker with an idempotent product effect because task delivery
is at least once.

## Verify

```sh
go mod tidy
go test ./...
go vet ./...
go build ./cmd/{{.ID}} ./cmd/{{.ID}}-worker
```

The integration test runs when `DATABASE_URL` is set. It uses
`MODARY_APPLICATION_SCHEMA` and `MODARY_QUEUE_SCHEMA` when supplied and proves
Preview, Execute, default deny, idempotent replay, SQL Audit, restart recovery,
and post-restart task consumption.
